{t: Spy Kiss}
{st: Medeski Martin and Wood}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 78}

{sot: Intro}
| Cm         | Cm         | Cm         | Cm         |
{eot}

{sot: Theme}
| Cm   Fm    | Cm   G7    | Cm   Fm    | Cm   G7    |
| Cm   Fm    | Cm   G7    | Cm   Fm    | Cm   G7    |
{eot}

{sot: Bridge}
| Ab7  G7    | Cm         | Ab7  G7    | Cm         |
| Ab7  G7    | Cm   Fm    | Ab7        | G7         |
{eot}

{sot: Solo}
| Cm         | Cm         | Cm         | Cm         |
{eot}

{sov: Notes}
Spy Aesthetic: The track relies on a mid-tempo, chromatic noir groove in C minor.
Keep the accompaniment dark, sparse, and rhythmic.

Theme Movement: The main head moves between the root Cm line and rapid
stabs on Fm and G7 (often voiced as G7alt or G7#9) to capture the classic
cinematic spy theme tension.

Bridge Tension: The bridge section builds momentum using a chromatic dominant
walk-down from Ab7 to G7 before resolving back to the root Cm groove.

Solos and Vamp: The open solo sections bounce over a modal C minor / C
Dorian vamp. Use minor blues or Dorian scale choices for improvisation.
{eov}